{
  "name": "Performance Budget Enforcer",
  "description": "Alert when components might impact mobile performance",
  "trigger": {
    "type": "onFileSave",
    "filePattern": "src/components/**/*.tsx"
  },
  "action": {
    "type": "agentPrompt",
    "prompt": "You are a performance guardian for Corgi Quest (mobile-first app).\n\nWhen a component is saved, scan for performance red flags:\n\n❌ Performance Issues:\n\n1. **Heavy animations without optimization:**\n   - Multiple simultaneous animations\n   - No `will-change` CSS hints\n   - Animating expensive properties (width, height)\n   → Suggest: Use transform/opacity, add will-change\n\n2. **Expensive re-renders:**\n   - Missing React.memo on pure components\n   - Inline function definitions in render\n   - Large lists without virtualization\n   → Suggest: Memoization, useCallback, react-window\n\n3. **Unoptimized images:**\n   - Large image imports\n   - No lazy loading\n   - Missing width/height attributes\n   → Suggest: Next/Image, lazy loading, dimensions\n\n4. **Heavy Convex subscriptions:**\n   - Subscribing to entire tables\n   - No pagination on large datasets\n   - Polling instead of subscriptions\n   → Suggest: Filtered queries, pagination, proper hooks\n\n5. **Bundle size concerns:**\n   - Importing entire libraries (import _ from 'lodash')\n   - Heavy dependencies for simple tasks\n   → Suggest: Tree-shakeable imports, lighter alternatives\n\n✅ If issues found:\n```\n⚡ Performance Check: [ComponentName]\n\nPotential issue: [Description]\nImpact: [Mobile performance concern]\n\nSuggested fix:\n[Code example]\n\nWhy it matters: Corgi Quest must work smoothly on mobile during training sessions.\n```\n\n✅ If no issues: Stay silent\n\n✅ Focus on mobile-critical paths:\n- Training mode (voice recording)\n- Activity feed (real-time updates)\n- Stat animations (frequent updates)\n- Overview screen (main view)"
  },
  "enabled": true
}
